>>
Rule 1 (argument must be a boolean literal)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = true ∨ v_1 = false
>>
Rule 2 (normalization to canonical boolean)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = (if v_1 then true else false)
>>
Rule 3 (mutual exclusivity of truth values)
{v_1 : bool} |= (v_1 = true ∧ v_1 ≠ false) ∨ (v_1 = false ∧ v_1 ≠ true)
>>
Rule 4 (quantified boolean domain check)
{v_1 : bool} |= ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1 = true ∨ v_1 = false
>>
Rule 5 (equivalence of negation and opposite literal)
{v_1 : bool} |= (if v_1 ≠ true then v_1 = false) ∧ (if v_1 = false then v_1 ≠ true)
